course: dictionary
lesson: 455
title: Finding meaning in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You do not need to know every word to understand a text. Read the words around an unknown word, because they are its context and they leave clues. «Genesis tells of Noah, a good man in a violent world, whom God told to build a huge wooden boat, the ark, for his family and pairs of every kind of animal.» The clues are huge wooden boat and animals, so ark must mean a boat.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The ark carried Noah's family and pairs of every kind of animal through the flood.» A boat carrying a family through a flood makes sense, so the meaning fits.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «In the story, rain fell for forty days and the waters covered the earth; everything outside the ark was lost.» The ark was the safe place, so the clues point to the boat again. When the clues are not enough, a dictionary will tell you every meaning.
fact: An ark is a large wooden boat in the Bible story of Noah.
fact: «The ark» carried Noah's family and pairs of every kind of animal through the flood.
fact: The Ark of the Covenant was a gold-covered wooden box that held the stone tablets of the Ten Commandments.
fact: In a synagogue, the ark (Holy Ark) is the cupboard where the Torah scrolls are kept.
fact: «Noah's Ark» can also mean a safe place that saves animals, as in «zoos keep rescue groups safe like a Noah's Ark».
exercise: «Genesis tells of Noah, a good man in a violent world, whom God told to build a huge wooden boat, the ark.» What was the ark? | A small toy car | A cupboard in a synagogue | *A huge wooden boat | A gold box for the stone tablets
exercise: «The ark carried Noah's family and pairs of every kind of animal through the flood.» Find and copy one word from this sentence that names the boat. | family | animal | *ark | flood
exercise: In a synagogue, what is the ark? | A gift for guests | A rainbow in the sky | *The cupboard where the Torah scrolls are kept | A wooden boat for animals
test: «The Ark of the Covenant» was a gold-covered wooden box. What did it hold? | *The stone tablets of the Ten Commandments | Pairs of every kind of animal | Bread from the oven | Rain water from the flood
test: «In the story, rain fell for forty days and the waters covered the earth; everything outside the ark was lost.» What happened to everything outside the ark? | *It was lost | It was found by Noah | It floated safely on the water | It was carried into the ark
exam: «Zoos keep rescue groups safe like a Noah's Ark.» In this sentence, what does Noah's Ark mean? | A type of fish | A dark cave under the sea | *A safe place that saves animals | A fast train
